.\" Makefile. CI fails if a Makefile bump lands without regenerating.
.\" Edit the .in for content changes; bumping just VERSION needs only
.\" the make target.
.TH MAC-GUEST-AGENT 8 "@DATE@" "mac-guest-agent @VERSION@" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mac-guest-agent \- QEMU Guest Agent for macOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mac-guest-agent
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mac-guest-agent
is a QEMU Guest Agent (QGA) implementation for macOS virtual machines. It
enables hypervisors (Proxmox VE, libvirt, QEMU) to manage macOS guests through
the standard QGA protocol over a serial port.
.PP
The agent communicates via an ISA serial port (16550 UART) that macOS supports
natively through the built-in Apple16X50Serial.kext driver. No
custom kernel extensions or SIP modifications are required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Run as a daemon. Log output goes to the log file instead of stderr.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Specify the serial device path. Default: auto-detect from known ISA paths
(/dev/cu.serial1, /dev/cu.serial2, /dev/cu.serial and tty equivalents).
VirtIO transport was removed in v2.5.0 \(em see CHANGELOG.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-logfile " " \fIPATH\fR
Log file path. Default: /var/log/mac-guest-agent.log when daemonized.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-pidfile " " \fIPATH\fR
PID file path.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-block\-rpcs " " \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated list of commands to disable. Example:
.B \-b guest-exec,guest-set-user-password
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-allow\-rpcs " " \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated list of commands to allow. All others are disabled.
Takes precedence over block-rpcs.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file path. Default: /etc/qemu/qemu-ga.conf
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-dump\-conf
Print effective configuration and exit.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Test mode. Uses stdin/stdout instead of a serial device. Does not require
QEMU or root privileges.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-install
Install as a macOS LaunchDaemon system service.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Remove the LaunchDaemon service and binary.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
When combined with \fB\-\-install\fR, \fB\-\-uninstall\fR, or \fB\-\-update\fR,
print every action the operation would take without touching the filesystem
or calling launchctl. Root is also skipped (no privileged operations
execute). Available v2.5.1+. Used by
.B scripts/install.sh \-\-dry\-run
for end-to-end smoke testing the install flow without affecting the host.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Run environment diagnostics and report readiness. Checks macOS version,
architecture, serial device availability, required tools, filesystem
capabilities, freeze hook validation, service status, and more.
Exits 0 if all checks pass, 1 if any fail.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The agent reads an optional configuration file at /etc/qemu/qemu-ga.conf
(compatible with the Linux qemu-ga format):
.PP
.RS
.nf
[general]
daemonize = 0
path = /dev/cu.serial1
logfile = /var/log/mac-guest-agent.log
verbose = 0
block-rpcs = guest-exec,guest-set-user-password
.fi
.RE
.SH HYPERVISOR SETUP
On Proxmox VE, set the guest agent to ISA serial mode:
.PP
.RS
.B qm set <vmid> --agent enabled=1,type=isa
.RE
.PP
Then stop and start the VM (QEMU args change requires a full restart).
ISA serial is the supported default transport on every macOS version
this agent targets (10.4 Tiger through current). On macOS 11.0 (Big
Sur) and later the VirtIO console channel is claimed by Apple's own
\fBAppleQEMUGuestAgent\fR on Virtualization.framework\-backed guests,
so \fItype=isa\fR (or the QEMU equivalent for non\-PVE hypervisors)
keeps this agent on a dedicated channel.
.SH SUPPORTED COMMANDS
The agent registers 42 QGA commands including aliases, macOS-specific
approximations, and documented deviations from Linux qemu-ga.
See docs/COMMAND_STATUS.md for per-command details.
.PP
See
.B mac-guest-agent --test
for interactive testing of all commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/mac-guest-agent
Agent binary.
.TP
.I /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.macos.guest-agent.plist
LaunchDaemon configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/qemu/qemu-ga.conf
Optional configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/log/mac-guest-agent.log
Log file.
.TP
.I /etc/newsyslog.d/mac-guest-agent.conf
Log rotation configuration.
.SH SECURITY
The agent runs as root and accepts commands from the hypervisor via the
serial port. The security model assumes the hypervisor is trusted. Sensitive
commands (guest-exec, guest-set-user-password, guest-ssh-*) can be
disabled via block-rpcs or allow-rpcs.
.PP
Passwords are passed to dscl via stdin, not on the command line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Error (device not found, permission denied, etc).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qemu-ga (8),
.BR launchctl (1),
.BR dscl (1)
